From: Nilanka de Silva <nilankadsilva@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: credit a client poll ACK to the STA on its own link

The driver reports the ACK of a client poll (NL80211_CMD_PROBE_CLIENT)
on the BSS that owns the driver context, which for an AP MLD is the
first affiliated AP. hostapd_client_poll_ok() looks the STA up on that
BSS and on the other BSSes of the same interface only, so the ACK of a
STA associated with another affiliated AP is dropped: the inactivity
poll of that STA never counts as answered and ap_handle_timer()
disassociates it after the next timeout although it is present and
reachable. hostapd_event_sta_low_ack() already resolves the STA across
the affiliated APs; do the same for the poll ACK.

Observed on mt7996 (OpenWrt, hostapd 2026-08-07) with non-MLO clients on
the second link of a two-link AP MLD: the kernel reports every poll as
acknowledged (driver TX status ACK), hostapd never logs AP-STA-POLL-OK
for them, and idle clients on that link are dropped for inactivity.
Clients on the first link are credited normally.

Signed-off-by: Nilanka de Silva <nilankadsilva@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -2819,6 +2819,18 @@
 					data->eapol_tx_status.link_id);
 		break;
 	case EVENT_DRIVER_CLIENT_POLL_OK:
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+		if (hapd->conf->mld_ap &&
+		    !ap_get_sta(hapd, data->client_poll.addr)) {
+			struct hostapd_data *p_hapd;
+
+			p_hapd = hostapd_find_by_sta(hapd->iface,
+						     data->client_poll.addr,
+						     false, NULL);
+			if (p_hapd)
+				hapd = p_hapd;
+		}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 		hostapd_client_poll_ok(hapd, data->client_poll.addr);
 		break;
 	case EVENT_RX_FROM_UNKNOWN:
